    "b-ks2-src-intro": {
      "id": "b-ks2-src-intro",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A knowledge source stores raw material cited by the knowledge graph. Every "
        },
        {
          "insert": "evidence",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row and every "
        },
        {
          "insert": "link",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " carries a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "kind",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and a typed "
        },
        {
          "insert": "locator",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " that resolves to one record in one source. Sources hold records, and the graph holds claims. Citations use locators rather than foreign keys to source rows, with one pointer mechanism across five heterogeneous sources. Reverse lookup finds claims supported by a record through an indexed query on "
        },
        {
          "insert": "(kind, locator)",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Display resolves a locator into its source at read time; no content snapshot is stored on the citing row."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-classes-heading": {
      "id": "b-ks2-src-classes-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Two Classes"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-src-classes-table": {
      "id": "b-ks2-src-classes-table",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Class",
          "Sources",
          "Contract"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Archival",
            "Discord, pull requests, wiki",
            "Captured inputs remain immutable once imported. Initial Sync seeds configured sources. Incremental Sync follows each source's refresh policy: PR and Discord refresh through their configured adapters, while wiki imports a local export on an explicit refresh. New captures preserve existing citation identities."
          ],
          [
            "Operational",
            "Attempts, code",
            "Attempts provide evidence from the target ledger. Runs, submissions, and transcripts grow with every run and are immutable once written. Code is the active checkout and the only drifting source. Its citations carry a required digest."
          ]
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
