    "source-contract-3": {
      "id": "source-contract-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Acquisition captures raw inputs. Import normalizes archival records. Search indexing makes records retrievable. Librarian backfill curates facts and relationships with citations. Backfill is not a synonym for download or import; each stage records completion independently."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "source-contract-4": {
      "id": "source-contract-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Rerunning the same capture must not duplicate records or work. Partial fetches retain resumable cursors without advancing past gaps. Changed upstream text creates a new capture while existing citations remain resolvable. Keep source data game-scoped; reusable cross-game facts require explicit applicability."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "source-contract-5": {
      "id": "source-contract-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Both initial/manual Sync and automatic epoch Sync call the configured source pipeline. It records acquisition, import, search indexing, and optional curation separately. Mechanical report reconciliation and attempt intake remain explicit lanes."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "source-contract-6": {
      "id": "source-contract-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Configured source pipeline",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "apps/server/src/core/knowledge-v2/ingest/game-sources.ts"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "source-contract-7": {
      "id": "source-contract-7",
      "type": "code",
      "props": {
        "annotations": [
